      "message": "I wonder if there is something going on here related to `CONFIG_ZEPHYR` and `CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX`. Although it shouldn\u0027t make a difference, from poking around the code I would expect that if `CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX` were defined then we would want to use `#include \u003cunistd.h\u003e` directly rather than including the path. It probably won\u0027t fix anything but it\u0027s probably better to be more explicit. Something like this:\n\n```\n#if defined(CONFIG_ZEPHYR) \u0026\u0026 !defined(CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX) \n#include \u003czephyr/posix/unistd.h\u003e\n#else\n#include \u003cunistd.h\u003e\n#endif\n\n#ifndef CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX\ntypedef long unsigned int __useconds_t;\n#endif\n```",
